    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d462">

                <pb facs="0693" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/2470: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-11-11T17:00:00+02:00">November 11,
                            1935—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 11—1:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>93. In accordance with the instructions of his Government, Italian Minister
                    yesterday made a verbal protest<anchor n="32" xml:id="d462-f1"/> against the
                    decision of the Egyptian Government in principle to apply sanctions against
                    Italy. Italian Minister is reported to have stated by an official announcement
                    of the Government of Egypt that the Italian Government reserved the right to
                    take any action which might be deemed necessary against Egypt in the event of
                    the violation of the latter’s international engagements with Italy.</p>
                <p>Repeated to American Embassy at Rome.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d462-f1" n="32" xml:id="d462-f1-content">
                <p>In despatch No. 424, of November 19, the Chargé corrected this statement and
                    reported that the Italian protest was communicated by written note
                    (765.84/3028).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
